# Rust / Tauri adapter

## Boundaries

- `crates/*-core`: product domains, safety, scan/cleanup — **no Tauri**.
- `crates/*-platform`: OS facts and capabilities — **no product orchestration**.
- `src-tauri/src/commands`: thin async adapters only.

## Commands

- Validate transport input → call Core → map typed errors.
- Emit progress events from Core callbacks; never invent UI strings in Rust for control flow.
- Register command + capability + frontend service binding in the same change.
- Prefer `deny_unknown_fields` + camelCase serde for FE payloads.
- Startup: no long filesystem work before first window paint.
- Fast/no-hang: blocking Core work only via `spawn_blocking`/`run_blocking`; emit progress; support cancel; return typed `operationBusy` instead of deadlocking.

## Safety

- Destructive ops: preview/dry-run, protected paths, explicit confirmation, verification.
- Privileged Windows APIs need an explicit capability boundary.
- Logs: operation IDs, counts, timings — not full private paths or file contents.

## Anti-patterns

- Scan/cleanup algorithms inside `#[tauri::command]`
- Catch-all `utils` / `manager` modules spanning unrelated domains
- Expanding Tauri permissions "just in case"
